  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Combi waste - stakeholder mapping study</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This study, under the combi-track &quot;Waste management&quot; in India, will give a full overview of relevant stakeholders involved in the Indian waste management sector in Ghaziabad, Mumbai, Muzaffarnagar and Nagpur and an in-depth analysis of their specific stakes.The aim within the combi-track on waste management is to create a conducive enabling environment, in order to improve waste management and recycling value chains in the above-mentioned locations and promote and support consortia of Dutch and Indian partners who want to work together.The study is conducted specifically for the combi-track to shed light on relevant stakeholders and their specific stakes in the waste management system in these locations, and give an overview of the local context, market dynamics and waste value chain.Following the study, the required interventions will be formulated and identified in the value chain to reach the objectives of the combi track and the Netherlands government will be able to determine which of these interventions could be provided by the Netherlands.</narrative>
  </description>
